## 11. SECURITY AND PRIVACY

Threat model: every server in the list may be malicious, hostile or compromised; mirrors/CDNs may be
tampered with; list contents may be crafted to exploit the parser.
- Integrity: signed manifest, rollback protection, strict validation (5.6, 6.3).
- Parser/config injection: typed builders only; allowlists for every field; length and charset
  limits; no filenames or shell commands derived from config content; use hash IDs as keys.
- Network pivoting: reject private/loopback/link-local targets before and after DNS resolution.
- Resource exhaustion: caps on download size, JSON depth, server count, field length, parse time,
  probe concurrency and total probing time.
- Untrusted exit: warn once (section 10), refuse plaintext/insecure configs (5.4), run the integrity
  canary in the pipeline, send no identifiers or credentials to servers, and make no privacy claims
  ("anonymous", "secure") in the UI.
- Local exposure: no new unauthenticated local listeners; any temporary probe inbound is
  loopback-only with random port and credentials and lives only for the probe.
- Secrets: signing key only in GitHub Actions secrets; the APK contains public keys only; CI jobs
  that touch untrusted data have no secrets; actions pinned by SHA.
- Logging: no full hosts, UUIDs, passwords or configs in release logs. Refer to servers as
  `id.take(8)`. Debug builds may keep an in-memory ring buffer of orchestrator decisions (state
  transitions, reasons, scores) without sensitive fields.
- Telemetry: none. Network requests go only to the configured mirrors and the probe endpoints.
- VpnService compliance: no traffic inspection, injection or ad behavior; collect no user traffic
  data.

## 12. RELIABILITY, PERFORMANCE AND BATTERY

- No heavy work on the main thread; lazy initialization; app startup time must not regress.
- Bounded concurrency everywhere; every network call has a timeout; every retry loop has backoff
  with jitter; no tight loops.
- Opportunistic warm-up: when the Free VPN screen opens and the cache is fresh, you may pre-test the
  top ~8 candidates once (cooldown 5 min, skipped under battery saver, skipped while a tunnel is up)
  so Connect is near-instant. No other background probing.
- Handle Doze/App Standby, process death, service restarts (same approach as the existing service),
  low memory and Android 12+ foreground-service restrictions the way the existing engine does.
- Release safety: add R8/ProGuard keep rules for any serialization classes you introduce and verify
  that the release (minified) build still parses the manifest.
- Memory: parse the manifest once, keep compact models, release probe instances immediately.

